-names>I</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Morphological and functional changes after intravitreal triamcinolone acetonide for retinal vein occlusion</article-title><source>Acta Ophthalmol Scand</source><volume>81</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>401</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12859269</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-co-2-269"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edelman</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lutz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Castro</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Corticosteroids inhibit VEGF-induced vascular leakage in a rabbit model of blood-retinal and blood-aqueous barrier breakdown</article-title><source>Exp Eye Res</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15670803</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-co-2-269"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Simpson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A randomized clinical trial of a single dose of intravitreal triamcinolone acetonide for neovascular age-related macular degeneration: One-year results</article-title><source>Arch Ophthalmol</source><volume>121</volume><fpage>667</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12742844</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-co-2-269"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jonas</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Degenring</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kreissig</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-g